# AwazPay — optional environment configuration
#
# Nothing in this file is required. The app runs fully without it, using the
# browser's built-in speech recognition (Settings -> Developer / Demo Mode ->
# Speech Provider -> Browser Speech Recognition).
#
# VITE_CLOUD_STT_PROXY_URL
#   Set this to point Cloud Speech-to-Text at a backend proxy instead of
#   calling a transcription API directly from the browser. When this is set,
#   no API key is ever sent to or stored in the browser: the proxy holds the
#   credential server-side. See server/sttProxy.example.mjs for a minimal
#   example of what such a proxy looks like, and README.md for how to run it.
#
#   Example:
#   VITE_CLOUD_STT_PROXY_URL=http://localhost:8787/transcribe
#
# Without this variable set, choosing Cloud Speech-to-Text in Settings falls
# back to calling the configured endpoint directly from the browser with a
# developer-entered key held in memory for the current tab only. That
# fallback exists purely so this can be tried in a few minutes for a
# hackathon demo; it is not how a shipped product should call a paid API.
